            0.652,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Arithmetic Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.086,
            0.847,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": "For each of the cases below, write the expression and identify its terms: If the teacher had called out ‘4’, Ruby would write If the teacher had called out ‘7’, Ruby would write Write expressions like the above for your class size."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.188,
            0.848,
            0.265
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "? Example 9: Raghu bought 100 kg of rice from the wholesale market and packed them into 2 kg packets. He already had four 2 kg packets. Write an expression for the number of 2 kg packets of rice he has now and identify the terms."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.269,
            0.845,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": "He had 4 packets. The number of new 2 kg packets of rice is $1 0 0 \\div 2 ,$ which we also write as $\\frac { 1 0 0 } { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.316,
            0.835,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": "The number of 2 kg packets he has now is $4 + { \\frac { 1 0 0 } { 2 } } ,$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.354,
            0.597,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.412,
            0.845,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 10:** Kannan has to pay ₹432 to a shopkeeper using coins of ₹1 and ₹5, and notes of ₹10, ₹20, ₹50 and ₹100. How can he do it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.456,
            0.658,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "There is more than one possibility. For example,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.48,
            0.679,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "432=4\\times100+1\\times20+1\\times10+2\\times1",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.503,
            0.845,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "Meaning: 4 notes of ₹100, 1 note of ₹20, 1 note of ₹10 and 2 notes of ₹1 432 = 8 × 50 + 1 × 10 + 4 × 5 + 2 × 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.552,
            0.832,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "Meaning: 8 notes of ₹50, 1 note of ₹10, 4 notes of ₹5 and 2 notes of ₹1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.58,
            0.633,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "Identify the terms in the two expressions above."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.611,
            0.768,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "? Can you think of some more ways of giving ₹432 to someone?"
        },
        {
